WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.210
- The internet is full of
fun and inspiring stories.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.290
Once you, you know, delete all the trolls.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.370
I find the best of the
best and present them here.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:08.203
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:08.203 --> 00:00:09.207
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.207 --> 00:00:11.350
(audience cheers)

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.140
So check out these photos, y'all.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.889
It looks like delicious
breakfast cereal, right?

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:17.740
I know, like childhood, right?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.090
Maybe some Fruit Loops, some Trix.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:19.923
I don't know.

00:00:19.923 --> 00:00:21.100
It's your dealer's choice.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.340
Well, it's the internet people.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.710
So of course, that's wrong.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:24.543
They're candles.

00:00:24.543 --> 00:00:26.318
They're actual frickin' candles.

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:29.043
And the best part is they actually smell

00:00:29.043 --> 00:00:29.876
(Kelly inhales)

00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:30.709
like the real thing.

00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:31.542
And I would know.

00:00:31.542 --> 00:00:32.375
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:35.930
These are the creation of
a 23 year old entrepreneur

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.393
who's documenting his entire
business journey on TikTok.

00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:40.217
Say hi to Kobe, y'all.

00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:41.210
(audience claps)

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.043
Hi, Kobe!

00:00:42.043 --> 00:00:42.876
- Hey!

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.709
Hello.

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.030
- I mean, well done with the smell.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.200
It smells just like it.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.033
It's crazy.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.800
So, you're very young to
like, start a business.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.190
So, how long have you been making candles?

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:55.330
- I have been making
candles for eight years now.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.267
I started back when I was 15 years old.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.930
I always knew I wanted
to start my own business.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.420
And so, I took entrepreneurship
class in high school.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.870
And after that, I thought, why wait?

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.800
And so, my freshman year of high school

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.192
I started Ardent Candle.

00:01:09.192 --> 00:01:11.230
And now, eight years later,

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.806
it's grown into a million dollar business,

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.542
hires 10 full-time employees.
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:18.462
And we have a 5,000 square foot warehouse.

00:01:18.462 --> 00:01:20.104
It's just been insane.

00:01:20.104 --> 00:01:21.920
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.231
Way to take a class
seriously is all I'm saying.

00:01:24.231 --> 00:01:26.670
So wait, you say that
your parents are probably

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.090
your biggest supporters, right?

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:29.923
- Yeah.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.607
My parents had a huge impact
on this whole journey.

00:01:32.607 --> 00:01:34.980
Growing up, my parents were entrepreneurs.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.730
So, I looked up to that.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.500
Like, when I was in school
and people would say,

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:39.680
what do you wanna be when you grow up?

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.450
I was always saying, I wanna be the boss

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.451
'cause that's my parents did.

00:01:42.451 --> 00:01:45.283
And when I was starting my business,

00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:48.267
my dad actually told me if
I wrote a business plan,

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.980
he would gimme the
money I needed to start.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:51.813
So I did that.

00:01:51.813 --> 00:01:54.985
My dad gave me 200 bucks and
that's how the company started.

00:01:54.985 --> 00:01:58.460
And my mom played a
huge part in my business

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:01.220
growing to where it is today
because once I started going

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.440
super viral on TikTok,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.927
I was also a full time college student

00:02:03.927 --> 00:02:06.483
and I wasn't gonna be able
to manage all of that.

00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:09.750
But my mom came to me
and said, look, Kobe,

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.454
I know this is what you wanna do

00:02:11.454 --> 00:02:14.867
and it might make sense for
you to take a break from school

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.750
to focus on your business.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.760
And that's not a typical parent's response

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.410
but I'm like, so grateful
that my mom, you know,

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.960
said that to me 'cause it
- Yeah!

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.080
- really helped me take the leap and go

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.130
and now it's grown to something so big,

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.590
bigger than we all ever thought.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:30.423
- Absolutely.

00:02:30.423 --> 00:02:31.730
And sometimes college is all about

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.110
you don't know what
you wanna do, you know?

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.140
So it helps you figure that out.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.850
And if you do know what
you wanna do, it's kind of,

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.480
it's important to focus on that dream.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.170
So thank you so much, Kobe.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.550
You've got great parents as well.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:41.383
Way to go.

00:02:41.383 --> 00:02:42.216
(audience claps)

00:02:42.216 --> 00:02:43.781
I'm liking your post right
now, along with your candle.

00:02:43.781 --> 00:02:44.880
(heart dings)

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:45.713
And that's not all.

00:02:45.713 --> 00:02:47.379
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:50.370
the go-to pen of the Kelly
Clarkson Show, wants to

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.720
honor ultimate overachievers
just like you, sir.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.025
So they're gonna be writin'
you a check for $1,000.

00:02:55.025 --> 00:02:55.858
How's that sound?

00:02:55.858 --> 00:02:56.691
(audience cheers)

00:02:56.691 --> 00:02:58.016
- Oh, wow!

00:02:58.016 --> 00:02:58.849
Thank you!

00:02:58.849 --> 00:02:59.682
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:59.682 --> 00:03:00.847
- You are killin' it, Kobe.

00:03:02.541 --> 00:03:03.374
- That's insane.

00:03:03.374 --> 00:03:04.624
Thank you so much.

00:03:04.624 --> 00:03:05.457
- Absolutely.

00:03:05.457 --> 00:03:07.653
Keep making these candles.
They smell delicious.

